      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. Let me write an improved version with clearer variable names, a descriptive method name, and comments explaining the intent.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces cryptic auto-generated variable names with descriptive ones (`defaultCodec`, `headerBytes`, `byteSource`, `bandHeaders`, `populationCodec`), renames the test method to `test_getCodec_populationCodecSpecifier_consumesAllStreamBytes`, and adds a Javadoc comment explaining why value 166 triggers a PopulationCodec path and why the `ByteArrayInputStream` reports zero bytes available after reading through the `BufferedInputStream`."
